ews.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxNZUVYamNZenk4WWpaVGpWdWVqaEhEMkpaZXdXS3hEU2dxclRLRGpYRUFSdmxXeFhCOHhsaUxMWHU4MGVPZHlrSVdkaEtoLXpjWGFDcG5KakVyazUzalBNU1Q3cEQ1aGJaQUtnWDk2dlBrUnQyYzBKQlRNZ0xJOEd1QlBSanM3Q0ZyWmJRcHhNalZCa25XNGQzT0Vpd1ptVmVaNktMamc1S0RuTkhZaWFWakZn?oc=5","date":"2026-11-06","zh":"Oklo 飆升 16%，因第三季虧損小於預期，選舉拋售引發反彈"},{"title":"Oklo (NYSE: OKLO) Stock Trades Near Its Cash Value As Dilution Concerns Mount Ahead Of Friday Earnings","src":"Foreign Policy Journal","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","date":"2026-11-06","zh":""},{"title":"NuScale Power Rises 7% on Doosan Manufacturing Deal; Oklo and BWX Technologies Trail","src":"24/7 Wall St.","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixAFBVV95cUxPOHhtT1VYREQxMGZoc2x0LWtpWlVvR1UtN3ZqS0djZlZTR1d1MUh5c3RUajVHOURzSzVKZWhna3d5ZUdjREFqYzdhZzJvbTRIenZUSF9xcmFRNGFab2VydHg5cHhFbjFQMV9OY1N3Nk11SzZQa3ljMG85NU9MWTRHbUQ4dHBFTzFpTU1zcnRfWmZPRjc5Rm1nMlpobGxLTTVDeENRVUM1VXRXN2VGR1ZabVZCclJNbVhNZXVQelZQVk5wekpK?oc=5","date":"2026-10-29","zh":"斗山製造交易推動 NuScale Power 股價上漲 7%； Oklo 和 BWX 技術路線"}],"themes":[{"name":"財報","count":5},{"name":"訂單/合約","count":4},{"name":"能源/電力","count":3},{"name":"分析師評等","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-03-17","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1849056/000162828026018698/oklo-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"We founded Oklo in 2013 with the goal of revolutionizing the energy landscape by developing clean, reliable, affordable energy solutions at scale. According to the International Energy Agency, global electricity production is expected to increase over 75% by 2050 driven by electrification of buildings, transportation, and industry; increased use of air conditioning in the developing world; and increased consumption from data centers and cloud services. Our business addresses this demand by producing electricity and heat from our Aurora powerhouses which can run on fresh, recycled, or down-blended nuclear fuel. We are also commercializing nuclear fuel recycling technology that can convert used nuclear fuel into usable fuel for our powerhouses and those of others.","zh":null},{"en":"The fast fission reactor technology we are commercializing was demonstrated by the Experimental Breeder Reactor-II (\"EBR-II\"), a fast fission plant that was operated by the U.S. government for 30 years. Our powerhouse product line, called the \"Aurora,\" builds on this legacy of proven and demonstrated technology. Our Aurora powerhouse product line is designed with embedded safety features, to be able to run on fresh, recycled, or down-blended fuel, and to produce 15-75 megawatts electric (\"MWe\") and has the potential to expand powerhouse size to produce 100 MWe and higher. Because the Aurora powerhouses are designed to operate by harnessing the power of high-energy, or \"fast,\" neutrons, they are expected to be able to tap into the vast energy reserves remaining in existing used nuclear fuel from conventional nuclear power generation facilities, which only use approximately 5% of the energ","zh":null},{"en":"We have achieved several significant deployment and regulatory milestones for our first Aurora powerhouse. Notably, we secured a site use permit from the U.S. Department of Energy (\"DOE\") for the Idaho National Laboratory (\"INL\") site and received a fuel award of five metric tons of HALEU produced from recovered uranium from previously irradiated EBR-II fuel from INL for a commercial Aurora powerhouse in Idaho. Related to the construction and operating licensing process of the Aurora powerhouse, we have also submitted the Nuclear Safety Design Agreement and the Preliminary Documented Safety Analysis to the DOE for the Aurora powerhouse at INL (\"Aurora-INL\"), which represent the first two of five steps in the DOE regulatory pathway for nuclear facility operation. Early in 2026, the DOE approved the Nuclear Safety Design Agreement. Related to our first Aurora powerhouse, the DOE and the IN","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"Our competitors include other power generation technologies, including traditional baseload power producers, other advanced nuclear technologies, renewables with or without storage, advanced energy storage, fossil fuels with carbon capture, and combinations of these technologies.","zh":null},{"en":"Fossil fuels with carbon capture — Sources provide firm, baseload power but require carbon capture technology to provide clean power. Carbon capture has not been demonstrated to be economically scalable.","zh":null}],"segments":{},"peers":["SMR","NNE","CRWV","NBIS","VST"]}}